        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for reply!\r\n\r\nI can help with a reproducible example. It only happens once in this case, after trigger this bug, if you press `hl`, which reenter the target directory, the behavior becomes normal.\r\n\r\nIf you adjust your nvim window to smaller that can only display two minifiles window, then it will be easier to reproduce.\r\n![mini files-bug2](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/30885216/797afae7-938d-4246-9bbf-8159b8fa388a)\r\nAnd some other factors might be related to this variable, https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d330f2639462084d2ef6c699ccd6219b81c45bc7/lua/mini/files.lua#L1315\r\nIn my opinion, the `win_id` was mistakenly set to nil in the following for loop because this wrong value of `depth_range.to`.\r\n",
